🔐 Hands-on 1 — Create an Opaque Secret 🔐

- If you create a Kubernetes Secret and don't specify type, Kubernetes uses opaque by default.
- We'll first create a Secret, inspect it, and decode the value.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 01 — Encode the secrets

# echo -n "admin" | base64
YWRtaW4=

# echo -n "password@123" | base64
cGFzc3dvcmRAMTIz

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 02 - Create the Secret

secret.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: app-secret
type: Opaque
data:
  DB_USERNAME: YWRtaW4=
  DB_PASSWORD: cGFzc3dvcmRAMTIz


# kubectl apply -f secret.yaml
secret/app-secret created


# kubectl describe secret app-secret
Name:         app-secret
Namespace:    default
Labels:       <none>
Annotations:  <none>

Type:  Opaque

Data
====
DB_PASSWORD:  12 bytes
DB_USERNAME:  5 bytes


# kubectl get secrets
NAME         TYPE     DATA   AGE
app-secret   Opaque   2      28s

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 03 — See the Base64 value

# kubectl get secret app-secret -o yaml

apiVersion: v1
data:
  DB_PASSWORD: cGFzc3dvcmRAMTIz
  DB_USERNAME: YWRtaW4=
kind: Secret
metadata:
  annotations:
    kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration: |
      {"apiVersion":"v1","data":{"DB_PASSWORD":"cGFzc3dvcmRAMTIz","DB_USERNAME":"YWRtaW4="},"kind":"Secret","metadata":{"annotations":{},"name":"app-secret","namespace":"default"},"type":"Opaque"}
  creationTimestamp: "2026-10-04T08:26:45Z"
  name: app-secret
  namespace: default
  resourceVersion: "80908"
  uid: ca5f3db6-96b0-4982-ba38-2f65710f5359
type: Opaque


Now decode it:
# kubectl get secret app-secret -o jsonpath='{.data.DB_PASSWORD}' | base64 --decode
password@123

# kubectl get secret app-secret -o jsonpath='{.data.DB_USERNAME}' | base64 --decode
admin

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What we just proved

Secret
  │
  ├── DB_USERNAME → Base64
  └── DB_PASSWORD → Base64

